{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Queen Sweetheart: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja66'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 66 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Itthivagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Women </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>6. Mudulakkhaṇajātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Queen Sweetheart: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Ekā icchā pure āsi, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>One wish I had in the past, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>aladdhā mudulakkhaṇaṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>before I won Queen Sweetheart. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Yato laddhā aḷārakkhī, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>But when I won the moon-eyed lady, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>icchā icchaṁ vijāyathā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>wish upon wish was born. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Mudulakkhaṇajātakaṁ chaṭṭhaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
